    "created_at": "2021-07-28T16:39:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-07-28T16:39:48Z",
    "body": "Thanks @camillelamy , implementing https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#the-rules-for-choosing-a-browsing-context-given-a-browsing-context-name (step 8) did indeed fix my failures on html/cross-origin-opener-policy/iframe-popup-same-origin-to-same-origin.https.html.\r\n\r\nHowever, it didn't fix my failures on html/cross-origin-opener-policy/iframe-popup-same-origin-allow-popups-to-same-origin-allow-popups.https.html because step 8 doesn't apply here, because COOP is \"same-origin-allow-popups\".\r\n\r\nI am failing this subtest for example:\r\n`FAIL same-origin-allow-popups with SAME_SITE iframe opening popup via window_open a SAME_SITE with COOP: \"same-origin-allow-popups\" assert_equals: opener expected false but got true`\r\n\r\nStep 8 for The rules for choosing a browsing context doesn't apply due to COOP value. I *think* that https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#check-browsing-context-group-switch-coop-value should imply no context group switch but the test is expecting a switch.\r\n\r\nWhen navigating the popup from about:blank to SAME_SITE origin, I believe both activeDocumentCOOPValue & responseCOOPValue are \"same-origin-allow-popups\". I also believe that both activeDocumentNavigationOrigin & responseOrigin are the SAME_SITE origin. Therefore, I would expect no switch. Am I wrong about that?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/888456341/reactions",
