    "created_at": "2021-07-29T15:28:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-07-29T15:28:25Z",
    "body": "I see, that makes sense and I was able to update WebKit accordingly.\r\n\r\nI found one more test that seems to disagree with https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/origin.html#check-browsing-context-group-switch-coop-value though:\r\n- imported/w3c/web-platform-tests/html/cross-origin-opener-policy/navigate-top-to-aboutblank.https.html (last subtest)\r\n\r\nIts comment says:\r\n> // Same origin allow popups allows the navigation of top to the cross-origin\r\n> // about:blank (origin inherited from the iframe) page, which does not have COOP\r\n> // (initiator is a cross origin iframe).\r\n\r\nAs far as I can tell, an iframe of origin B is trying to navigate its top-frame of origin A to about:blank (which would resolve to origin B). The top frame has COOP=\"same-origin-allowing-popups\" and responseCOOP should be \"unsafe-none\" because about:blank (because navigation initiator is a cross-origin iframe).\r\n\r\nThe spec says that:\r\n\r\n> If all of the following are true:\r\n> - isInitialAboutBlank,\r\n> - activeDocumentCOOPValue's value is \"same-origin-allow-popups\".\r\n> - responseCOOPValue is \"unsafe-none\",\r\n>\r\n> then return false.\r\n\r\nThe \"isInitialAboutBlank\" check would fail for this navigation. Therefore, I would expect a browsing context group switch but the subtest doesn't.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
